[SO-20583237] Q: OpenGL Shader ERROR: 0:1: '' : syntax error #version
A: <p>You can tell OSX to use a newer version of OpenGL by setting it in your pixel format when you create the context. <a href="https://stackoverflow.com/questions/8874997/setting-up-and-using-opengl-3-0-with-mac-osx-lion10-7">Here is an example</a> of how to set it up.</p>

<p>Or if you're using glut, I think you want <code>glutInitContextVersion(x, y);</code> where <code>x</code> and <code>y</code> are the major and minor version numbers. GLSL 1.5 is supported in OpenGL 3.2, I think. (And you might also want <code>glutInitContextProfile(GLUT_CORE_PROFILE);</code>, I think.)</p>


