[SO-27528141] Q: How to setup proxy in Swift?
A: <p>The <code>CFProxySupport</code> framework allows your app to retrieve proxies that have been configured in the device.  Some of these proxy configurations may actually be a auto proxy config URL/script - so <code>CFNetworkCopyProxiesForURL</code> may evaluate these scripts to the determine the proxies that apply to the specified URL.</p>

<p><code>CFProxySupport</code> does not allow you to configure the proxies that the device will use.  Further, <code>NSURLConnection</code> doesn't honour the device proxy settings.  You can use the code you have to retrieve the configured proxy and then use this with a library, such as NSURLSession or AFNetworking, that does support the use of a proxy server.  In NSURLSession you specify the proxy configuration in the <code>connectionProxy</code> dictionary of the <a href="https://developer.apple.com/library/ios/documentation/Foundation/Reference/NSURLSessionConfiguration_class/index.html#//apple_ref/occ/instp/NSURLSessionConfiguration/connectionProxyDictionary" rel="nofollow">NSURLSessionConfiguration</a> object</p>


