Q: MemoryManagement
A: <p>iOS does not support Garbage Collection. Garbage collection would remove any objects which no longer have any references to them. On the iOS if you have no references to an object that space in memory will be lost and you'll have a memory leak.</p>

<p><code>autoRelease</code> tells an object to release in the very near future. This is useful in certain cases, such as returning an object created in a function, where you will not be able to release it.</p>

<p>e.g.:</p>

<pre>
+ (id) createNewObject {
    id *newObject = [[Object alloc] init];
    [newObject autoRelease];
    return newObject;
}
</pre>

<p>In this case the object calling this function would have to retain the object that is returned so it is not removed from memory.</p>

llm_answer:
Garbage collection is not supported for iPhone applications. Instead, memory management is handled through Automatic Reference Counting (ARC) or manual reference counting using retain, release, and autorelease commands. The retrieved sources indicate that on iOS, if there are no references to an object, that space in memory can be lost, leading to memory leaks [SO-5407738]. 

To replace the operations typically performed using `+alloc` and `-init` with garbage collection, you should use ARC. For example, the following code:

```objective-c
NSXMLParser *xmlParser = [[NSXMLParser alloc] initWithData:xmlData];
UIImage *originalImage = [[UIImage alloc] initWithData:data];
detailViewController = [[[DetailViewController alloc] initWithNibName:@"DetailView" bundle:[NSBundle mainBundle]] autorelease];
```

Would not work properly under garbage collection, as it is not available. Instead, with ARC, you would write:

```objective-c
NSXMLParser *xmlParser = [[NSXMLParser alloc] initWithData:xmlData];
UIImage *originalImage = [[UIImage alloc] initWithData:data];
detailViewController = [[DetailViewController alloc] initWithNibName:@"DetailView" bundle:[NSBundle mainBundle]];
```

In ARC, you do not need to call `autorelease`, `release`, or `retain`, as memory management is automated [SO-11163245][SO-5407738].

