        transitive = true
    }   
}
</code></pre>

<p>But if you want to use 22 SDK you should use such dependencies:</p>

<pre><code>repositories {
    maven { url "https://jitpack.io" }  
    }     

compile ('com.github.afollestad:material-dialogs:53103863a6') {
    transitive = true
}
</code></pre>

<p>This is the last version which supports 22 SDK - <strong>v. 0.6.4.4</strong>. But there is some problem with using old version number in dependency name (maybe because library author migrated to jCenter) and you can use first 10 digits of commit's hash related to <a href="https://github.com/afollestad/material-dialogs/releases/tag/v0.6.4.4" rel="nofollow">this version</a> instead.</p>

