Q: Close menu after clicking the menu link
A: <p>Same way you toggle it when you press the burger button.
The code needs to be on a function, to be <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Don%27t_repeat_yourself" rel="nofollow noreferrer">DRY</a></p>

<pre><code>var toggleMenu = function () {
  var burger = $(".hamburger-box");
  var overlay = $("#overlay");
  var menu = $('.js-nav').parent().find('.menu');

  burger.toggleClass("active");
  menu.toggleClass('active');
  overlay.toggle();
}

$(".hamburger-box, .js-nav a").on("click", toggleMenu);
</code></pre>

<p>The important part is <code>$(".hamburger-box, .js-nav a")</code> where you also bind the event to the links of the menu, and therefore the menu get closed.</p>

