<li>I found your question while searching the web for this idea for about 30 minutes. I would say that this doesn't appear to be a common solution.<br><br><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Demand_paging" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Demand paging</a> and <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Memory_overcommitment" rel="nofollow noreferrer">memory overcommitment</a> seem somewhat related to this idea though because they allow more memory to be allocated than what is actually resident in physical memory. Both of these are used commonly.</li>
</ol>


