Q: ExtJS 4.2.1 - reject changes in store after getting error from server
A: <p>the signature of the exception event is:</p>

<pre><code>exception( this, response, operation, eOpts )
</code></pre>

<p>where <code>this</code> is the proxy. you need to add a scope:</p>

<pre><code>listeners: {
    exception: function (proxy, response, operation) {
        var data = Ext.decode(response.responseText);
        Ext.MessageBox.show({
            title: 'Server error',
            msg: data.Message,
            icon: Ext.MessageBox.ERROR,
            buttons: Ext.Msg.OK
        });
        this.rejectChanges();
    },
    scope: this
}
</code></pre>

<p>It should work and in <code>this</code> should be the store.</p>

Q: ExtJS 4.2.1 - reject changes in store after getting error from server
A: <p>What about <a href="http://docs.sencha.com/extjs/4.2.1/#!/api/Ext.data.Model-method-reject" rel="nofollow">rejecting</a> each <a href="http://docs.sencha.com/extjs/4.2.1/#!/api/Ext.data.Operation-method-getRecords" rel="nofollow">record of the operation</a>, like this ?</p>

<pre><code>listeners: {
  exception: function(proxy, request, operation, eOpts){
    // ... any user notification ...

    Ext.each(operation.getRecords(), function(record){
      record.reject();
    });
  }
}
</code></pre>

<p>PS: This is valid for ExtJS 5.x as well (inside Base Model will be generally available for entire application) !</p>

Q: ExtJS 4.2.1 - reject changes in store after getting error from server
A: <p>This should be addressed from the controller. If the call to a sync method fails it will trigger an failure callback where you can reject changes.</p>

<pre><code>store.sync({
  failure : function(){
     store.rejectChanges();
  }
});
</code></pre>

Q: ExtJS 4.2.1 - reject changes in store after getting error from server
A: <p>Inside of your stores proxy add a listener for the exception. below is an example that on exception grabs the response msg and populates a pop up and rejects the changes. </p>

<pre><code>     listeners: {
             exception: function (proxy, response, operation, eOpts){
                 var data = Ext.decode(response.responseText);
                 Ext.MessageBox.alert('Error', 'The proxy event failed: &lt;br&gt;&lt;li&gt;'+data.errorMessage+'&lt;/li&gt;');
                 Ext.each(operation.getRecords(), function(record){
                     record.reject();
                 });
             }
         }
</code></pre>

