Q: Vue: Update part of an html string from data v-for loop with v-model input
A: <ol>
<li><code>name</code> should be in <code>data</code>, not in <code>props</code> (it's not coming from a parent, it's just reactive data, which needs to be tracked for changes internally - inside this component).</li>
<li><code>statements</code> should be in <code>computed</code>, because you want Vue to update it whenever its reactive references (e.g: <code>this.name</code>) change. Besides, <code>this</code> is not what you think it is inside the <code>data</code> function.</li>
</ol>
<p>See it working:</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="true" data-console="true" data-babel="false">
<div class="snippet-code snippet-currently-hidden">
<pre class="snippet-code-js lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>new Vue({
  el: "#app",
  data: () =&gt; ({
    name: 'Bob'
  }),
  computed: {
    statements() {
        return [
        {
          id: 'food',
          text: '&lt;b&gt;'+ this.name + '&lt;/b&gt; likes to eat ice cream.',
        },
        {
          id: 'fun',
          text: 'Runing is the favorite activity of &lt;b&gt;'+ this.name + '&lt;/b&gt;',
