Q: Why does my styled components transitions are not working?
A: <p>You can pass the property to your styled component like so:</p>
<p>JSX:</p>
<pre><code>return (
  &lt;BurgerStyled
    onClick={() =&gt; setIsBurgerOpen(!isBurgerOpen)}
    open={isBurgerOpen}
  &gt;
    &lt;span /&gt;
    &lt;span /&gt;
    &lt;span /&gt;
  &lt;/BurgerStyled&gt;
);
</code></pre>
<p>Style:</p>
<pre><code>const BurgerStyled = styled(({ open, ...restProps }) =&gt; &lt;div {...restProps} /&gt;)`
  ${({ open }) =&gt; open ? ` styles open here ` : ` styles closed here `};
`;
</code></pre>
<p>What you do here: you pass the <code>open</code> prop to your styled component, and then pass all other props to the div. The <code>open</code> prop is now available in your style template string. This prevents the <code>open</code> prop to be passed to the DOM-element, because a <code>&lt;div&gt;</code> DOM-element has no <code>open</code> property, so passing it through to the DOM would result in warnings.</p>

