4. **Redirect on Successful Login**: After successful authentication, redirect the user to the home page or another relevant area of your application. This is usually managed using `FormsAuthentication.SetAuthCookie()` as shown above ([SO-19066263]).

5. **Consider Additional Features**: Depending on your requirements, you may also want to implement features like user roles or manage login attempts to prevent brute-force attacks. You can use SQL scripts to create roles as needed ([SO-25420814]).

