You cannot directly inherit from multiple classes in C#, such as `ProfileBase`, `MembershipUser`, and `ISessionMgrEntry`, because C# does not support multiple class inheritance. The language allows inheritance from only one base class, which is the primary reason for the compiler error you are encountering when trying to declare:

```csharp
public class User : ProfileBase, MembershipUser, ISessionMgrEntry
```

To work around this limitation, you can use composition instead of inheritance. This is evident in the second code snippet you provided where you encapsulate instances of `MembershipUser` and `ProfileBase` within the `User` class. Here’s a suggested way to structure your `User` class:

```csharp
public class User
{
    private readonly MembershipUser _MembershipUser;
    private readonly ProfileBase _ProfileBase;

    public User()
    {
        _MembershipUser = new MembershipUser();
        _ProfileBase = new ProfileBase();
    }

    public string Comment
    {
        get { return _MembershipUser.Comment as string; }
        set { _MembershipUser.Comment = value; }
    }

    public bool IsAnonymous
    {
        get { return _ProfileBase.IsAnonymous as bool; }
    }

    // Implement additional members as needed
}
