Q: Angular add to favourites
A: <p>By using <code>scope: $scope</code> you are setting the scope to your surrounding controller scope, so all of your popups sharing the same <code>isFavourite</code> variable.</p>

<p>You could do something like this:</p>

<pre><code>&lt;div ng-repeat="item in items"&gt;
    &lt;button ng-click="addToFav(item)" ng-class="{'active' : item.isFavourite}"&gt;&lt;i class="ion-heart"&gt;&lt;/i&gt; Netto&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
</code></pre>

<p>controller:</p>

<pre><code>$scope.addToFav = function (item) {
    $ionicPopup.show({
        title: 'Tilføj til favoritter',
        subTitle: 'Ønsker du at tilføje denne butik til dine favoritter?',
        scope: $scope,
        buttons: [
            { text: 'Nej' },
            { text: '&lt;b&gt;Ja&lt;/b&gt;',
                type: 'button-positive',
                onTap: function(e) {
                    item.isFavourite = true;
                }
            }
        ]
    });
</code></pre>

