Q: Implementing Service Workers with an appcache fallback for unsupported browsers
A: <p>The check which technology the browser is supporting is easly done:</p>

<pre><code>if(navigator.serviceWorker){
    initServiceWorker()
}else if(window.applicationCache){
    initApplicationCache();
}else{
    console.log('no caching possible');
}
</code></pre>

<p>Dynamic loading a service worker should not be a problem since it is done in javascript anyway.</p>

<p>Dynamic loading applicationCache's mainfest seems not to be possible, but you can try an iframe hack, see:
<a href="https://stackoverflow.com/questions/4548342/dynamically-trigger-html5-cache-manifest-file">Dynamically Trigger HTML5 Cache Manifest file?</a></p>

