<p>The <em>current</em> version of the JSON specification allows the top level data type in the JSON text to be <strong>any</strong> JSON data type.</p>
<p>The <em>original</em> version only allowed an object or an array.</p>
<p>The error message says that having <code>&quot;</code> as the first character is an error, which implies that it doesn't support strings as the top level data type (and thus implements the original specification).</p>
