[SO-50588864] Q: ...Array(something) in JS
A: <p>The <code>... Array()</code> is what is known as a Spread Operator. This is used in arrays and objects to 'Spread' out their parts. In this case it is going through each member and creating an array Object with the value that you placed in there, the <code>props.ingredient[igKey]</code>.</p>

<p><code>props</code> in this case and in the case of React is the properties that have been passed to the component. So in the case of <code>&lt;Burger ingredient={this.state.ingredient}/&gt;</code> props contains ingredient.</p>

<p>So what you are ending up with is an array of Array objects there each the length of the corresponding value in <code>this.state.ingredient</code> that was passed in, such that when igKey is cheese it has created an Array object with the value assigned to cheese (2).</p>


