A: <p>Tables are for tabular data, if you want to layout content you should be using CSS.</p>

<p>I recommend using something like <a href="http://twitter.github.com/bootstrap/" rel="nofollow">Twitter Boostrap</a> if you struggling with the CSS.</p>

<p>If you really just want a specific solution have a look at the results for terms like <a href="http://www.google.co.uk/#hl=en&amp;q=css+3+column+layout+fluid+center&amp;sa=X&amp;ei=OuU0UJK6MIGH0AWN7YCoBg&amp;ved=0CE8Q7xYoAA&amp;bav=on.2,or.r_gc.r_pw.r_qf.&amp;fp=1eacde5ba99084b&amp;biw=1394&amp;bih=907" rel="nofollow">"css 3 column layout fluid center</a> - I am not fobbing you off with that, there really are great answers there that are exactly what you want, and lots of search results will take you to those pages (especially to the manisheriar.com and A List Apart articles).</p>

