Q: Dynamically edit a link to change video source
A: <p>Here is what worked for me thanks to @Tushar</p>

<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-js lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>$('#button').on({
    'click': function(){
    var inputvalue = $("#input").val();
    $('#videot').attr('src', "http://example.com/episode/" + inputvalue + "/something.mp4");
    }
});</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;div&gt;
&lt;input type="text" value="Episode Number" id="input"&gt;
&lt;button type="button" class='btn' id="button"&gt;Watch&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;video id='videot' width="100%" controls="controls"&gt;
&lt;source src="http://example.com/episode/25/something.mp4" type="video/mp4"&gt;
Your browser does not support this video's playback.&lt;/video&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>

Q: Toggle, show hide element on button or page click
A: <p>In this case the DIV has the id of DIV1 as you can see in the javascript. Just use javascript no jquery is needed, this is easier anyway.</p>

<pre><code>&lt;div class="moreDiv"&gt;More &lt;/div&gt;&lt;div  id="DIV1" class="hiddenDiv"&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Add favorites&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Give a Gift&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Block&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
</code></pre>

<p>Javascript:</p>

<pre><code>function ShowDIV(){
if (DIV1.style.display=="none") DIV1.style.display="block";
else DIV1.style.display="none";
}
</code></pre>

<p>Html to hid or show div:</p>

<pre><code>&lt;a href="#" onClick="ShowDIV();"&gt;&lt;button&gt;Show DIV&lt;/button&gt;&lt;/a&gt; 
</code></pre>

