The retrieved sources do not cover how to specifically change the title and URL in your script by clicking on a post in a WordPress archive page. However, I can suggest a general approach based on the use of event listeners and modifying object properties as detailed in the provided context.

1. **Using Event Listeners:** You can attach an event listener to each of your links. For instance, instead of having duplicate IDs (which should be unique in HTML), you could use a class since multiple elements would share the same functionality. You could modify your anchors like this:

    ```html
    <a href="link1" class="shareBtn" data-title="Title 1" data-url="https://example.com/link1">Title 1</a>
    <a href="link2" class="shareBtn" data-title="Title 2" data-url="https://example.com/link2">Title 2</a>
    ```

2. **Handling the Click Event:** You would then set up event listeners for all buttons with a class selector and within the event handler, retrieve the necessary data attributes for the URL and title:

    ```javascript
    document.querySelectorAll('.shareBtn').forEach(button => {
        button.addEventListener('click', event => {
            event.preventDefault(); // Prevent default link navigation
            const shareTitle = button.getAttribute('data-title');
            const shareUrl = button.getAttribute('data-url');

            if (navigator.share) {
                navigator.share({
                    title: shareTitle, // Using the title from data attribute
                    url: shareUrl // Using the URL from data attribute
                }).then(() => {
                    console.log('Thanks for sharing!');
                }).catch(err => {
                    console.log("Error while using Web share API:");
                    console.log(err);
                });
            } else {
                alert("Browser doesn't support this API !");
            }
        });
    });
    ```

This method will allow you to change the title and URL dynamically based on the link that was clicked, which aligns with the general principles discussed in the context provided. However, specifics regarding implementation within WordPress are not covered in the sources retrieved.

