To move promoted events to the top of the array in your Node.js function, you can modify the last filter method to instead collect the promoted events separately and then concatenate them with the rest of the non-promoted events. Here's an updated approach:

```javascript
// Remove duplicates and expired
var data = (result[0].concat(result[1]).concat(result[3])).filter((event, index, self) => self.findIndex((t) => {
